# tools/cp/p9/play.p9 -- Gate P9 boot A (lane C9-play, docs/cp-p9.md §3).
# Main menu -> LOAD GAME -> ManualSave-86 (the user's save, "The Ripperdoc",
# Megabuilding H10 atrium, Little China, Watson), ~11.5 min of play with QMP
# keyboard + relative mouse (walk, turn, sprint, map), F5 quick save, QUIT GAME.
# The sequences come from the interactive boot ctl1 (docs/cp-p9.md §2):
#  * menus: the focus is hidden until the first key; taps need ~0.8 s
#    spacing (boot_p9 `key` default); `seek` reads the highlighted row's
#    position from the screendump, so no tap count is trusted (gateA1: in the
#    main menu "up" past CONTINUE lands on the patch-notes button).
#  * LOAD GAME groups saves by playthrough; "0" expands every group; the
#    Ripperdoc group (ManualSave-86) is the last entry, above the
#    Cross Progression button.
#  * the save's world: walking forward from the start meets Jackie (a talk
#    trigger, not a choice); the street is behind and to the left.

phase menu
shot menu
# ---- LOAD GAME -> ManualSave-86 ---------------------------------------------
seek menu-load main down 6 LOAD GAME
key ret
expect loadlist 30 LOAD\s*GAME|Expand\s*groups|Coll\w*\s*groups|Progression
key 0
wait 2
# the list with both groups expanded (ctl1): Streetkid/AutoSave-16 group at
# the top, then the second Streetkid group whose one entry, "The Ripperdoc"
# (ManualSave-86), has its frame centred at screen row 509
expect loadlist-ripperdoc 10 Ripperdoc
listseek loadlist-focus down 8 509
phase loading
key ret
expect loaded 400 PRESS\b.{0,24}\bTO\s+CONTINUE
key spc
wait 6
phase world
expect inworld 60 RIPPERDOC|Jackie
shot world-start
prof 20 10 world-start

# ---- ~10 min in the world -------------------------------------------------------
# 1. walk to Jackie (dialogue trigger), look around
hold w 3000
look 500 0 25 16
wait 2
look -500 0 25 16
shot w1
# 2. turn around toward the street, walk and sprint
look 1200 0 40 16
hold w 4000
down shift
hold w 5000
up shift
shot w2
# 3. the map: open, look, close.  M usually opens the map, once (r2-play-put1)
#    the hub; Esc steps map -> hub -> world, so `unwind` presses Esc until no
#    map/hub text is left (gateA2 spent its loops in the hub).
phase map
key m
wait 5
shot map
unwind map-close 4 FILTER|Track\s*Waypoint|Zoom\s*out|SKIP\s*TIME|DATABASE|CYBERWARE|INVENTORY|JOURNAL|STREET\s*CRED|CHARACTER
phase world
# 4. a loop of walking / sprinting / looking (16 x ~20 s)
repeat 16
down shift
hold w 6000
up shift
look 350 0 15 16
hold w 4000
look -150 40 10 16
hold a 1500
hold d 1500
look 0 -40 5 16
wait 3
shot loop
end
prof 20 10 world-mid
# 5. backwards / strafing and a second map look
hold s 3000
hold a 3000
look -900 0 30 16
down shift
hold w 8000
up shift
phase map
key m
wait 5
shot map2
unwind map-close2 4 FILTER|Track\s*Waypoint|Zoom\s*out|SKIP\s*TIME|DATABASE|CYBERWARE|INVENTORY|JOURNAL|STREET\s*CRED|CHARACTER
phase world
# 6. another loop (16 x ~17 s)
repeat 16
hold w 5000
look 600 0 20 16
down shift
hold w 5000
up shift
look -300 0 10 16
wait 3
shot loop2
end
prof 20 10 world-end
wait 10
shot before-save

# ---- save, then QUIT GAME --------------------------------------------------------
phase save
key f5
wait 5
shot saved-place
wait 5
key esc
wait 4
shot pause
seek pause-quit pause down 9 QUIT GAME
exit_ok
phase quit
key ret
wait 3
shot quit-confirm
expect quit-confirm 10 sure.{0,20}quit
key ret
wait_exit 180
